    "problem_statement": "A new architecture primitive arch_cpu_irqs_are_enabled() must report the calling CPU's current interrupt-enable state without modifying it. Unlike arch_irq_unlocked(), which inspects a saved lock key, this primitive probes the live CPU register directly: it must return true when interrupts are enabled (thread context), false immediately after arch_irq_lock(), and true again after arch_irq_unlock(), and it must not alter the state it observes on either call. It must be available and behave correctly on the target architecture.",
